<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Direct Variation 2 - Price of maize</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The cost, \(C\), of maize varies directly as its mass, \(m\), in kilograms: \(C = km\).</p>
<p>(a) A trader in Eldoret sells \({@pm1@}\) kg of maize for Ksh \({@pC1@}\). Find the value of the constant \(k\) (the price per kilogram).</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Use your value of \(k\) to find the cost of \({@pm2@}\) kg of maize.</p>
<p>Cost = Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Substitute the known values into \(C = km\): \({@pC1@} = k({@pm1@})\).</p>
<p>So \(k = \frac{ {@pC1@} }{ {@pm1@} } = {@pk@}\).</p>
<p>Using \(C = {@pk@}m\) with \(m = {@pm2@}\): \(C = {@pk@}({@pm2@}) = {@pC2@}\) Ksh.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
